  "unlinkedArticulations": [],
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "57d26f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 0,
      "content": "General Information for Transfer Students",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "c8996f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Thank you for your interest in National University! National University, one of the largest private nonprofit universities in the United States, is committed to your success through our Whole Human Education approach. Flexible Learning on Your Terms National University's flexible four and eight-week online courses allow you to focus on one class at a time. With unlimited free tutoring, individual coaching, and a dedicated writing center, we provide the support you need to excel. NU accepts and reviews applications year-round, so you can start your classes as soon as next month, depending on your program of study and location of choice. To learn more about applying, visit our Admissions page or call (855) 355-6288. Additional Resources · NU Course Equivalency Site : See how your other previous courses or exams will transfer to NU. · ADT Degrees : Explore scholarship and degree pathways for CCC students with ADT degrees. · Financial Aid : Discover how our Financial Aid team can help you secure the necessary resources. · NU Catalog : For detailed policies and more information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Thank you for your interest in National University!</strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">National University, one of the largest private nonprofit universities in the United States, is committed to your success through our Whole Human Education approach.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Flexible Learning on Your Terms</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">National University's flexible four and eight-week online courses allow you to focus on one class at a time.&nbsp;With unlimited free tutoring, individual coaching, and a dedicated writing center, we provide the support you need to excel.&nbsp;NU accepts and reviews applications year-round, so you can start your classes as soon as next month, depending on your program of study and location of choice.&nbsp;To learn more about applying, visit our </span><a href=\"https://www.nu.edu/admissions/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Admissions page</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> or call (855) 355-6288.&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Additional Resources </strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://tes.collegesource.com/publicview/TES_publicview01.aspx?rid=721eee70-5b00-4cd1-ac03-b96130b4f23f&amp;aid=f99ff523-c77e-4502-967a-32c21611921e\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">NU Course Equivalency Site</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">:&nbsp;See how your other previous courses or exams will transfer to NU.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.nu.edu/admissions/undergraduate/transfer-information/adt-pathways/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">ADT Degrees</a>:<span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Explore scholarship and degree pathways for CCC students with ADT degrees.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.nu.edu/admissions/financial-aid-and-scholarships/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Financial Aid</a>:<span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Discover how our Financial Aid team can help you secure the necessary resources.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.nu.edu/catalog/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">NU Catalog</a>:<span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> For detailed policies and more information.</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "59d26f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "Understanding this Agreement",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "699a6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "This articulation agreement outlines the preparatory courses required in the major, based on quarter credit hours. National University courses are listed on the left, with their approved (articulated) transfer equivalents on the right. General education and campus requirements for all bachelor’s degrees are detailed in separate agreements, which can be accessed in ASSIST by selecting “General Education/Breadth” on the left panel. Additionally, NU accepts CSU GE Breadth, IGETC, and Cal-GETC certification to fulfill its GE requirements, except for at least one upper-division GE elective. NU allows a maximum of 12 semester units (18 quarter units) of vocational/technical coursework. Transfer courses noted with \"Limits Apply to Non-CSU Transferable Courses\" will count toward this limit. For more information on this and all degrees at National University, see Program Finder. Changes to this Agreement Major requirements are subject to change. Newly articulated courses are added on a rolling basis, and the articulation status of some courses may be revised or discontinued. For the most current information, please visit ASSIST every quarter and regularly consult with an academic counselor at NU or your institution.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">This articulation agreement outlines the preparatory courses required in the major, based on quarter credit hours.&nbsp;National University courses are listed on the left, with their approved (articulated) transfer equivalents on the right.&nbsp;General education and campus requirements for all bachelor’s degrees are detailed in separate agreements, which can be accessed in ASSIST by selecting “General Education/Breadth” on the left panel.&nbsp;&nbsp;Additionally, NU accepts CSU GE Breadth, IGETC, and Cal-GETC certification to fulfill its GE requirements, except for at least one upper-division GE elective.&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">NU allows a maximum of 12 semester units (18 quarter units) of vocational/technical coursework. Transfer courses noted with \"Limits Apply to Non-CSU Transferable Courses\" will count toward this limit.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For more information on this and all degrees at National University, see </span><a href=\"https://www.nu.edu/program-finder/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Program Finder.</a></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Changes to this Agreement</strong></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Major requirements are subject to change. Newly articulated courses are added on a rolling basis, and the articulation status of some courses may be revised or discontinued. For the most current information, please visit ASSIST every quarter and regularly consult with an academic counselor at NU or your institution.</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "2bcb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "Information Applicable to RN to Bachelor of Science in Nursing (RN-BSN) Program (Online)",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2ecb6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The RN to BSN Program is delivered in a 100% online format. Courses are 4 or 8 weeks in length. The program provides a foundation for professional nursing practice at the baccalaureate level. The RN to BSN program at National University is accredited by the American Association of Colleges of Nursing (AACN), and the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education, 655 K Street NW, Suite 750, Washington, DC 20001, 202-887-6791. Upon acceptance to the program, applicants will be required to provide proof of a current, active, and unencumbered RN license in the State of residence. *Additionally, in the practicum courses, practicum sites may require students to provide evidence of current, active professional liability, malpractice insurance coverage for practicum courses, and provide evidence of a current AHA Healthcare Provider BLS CPR Card.\" For information about the program and how to obtain the RN to BSN Program application, students should email the Admissions Coordinator at RNCompletion@nu.edu",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The RN to BSN Program is delivered in a 100% online format. Courses are 4 or 8 weeks in length. The program provides a foundation for professional nursing practice at the baccalaureate level. The RN to BSN program at National University is accredited by the American Association of Colleges of Nursing (AACN), and the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education, 655 K Street NW, Suite 750, Washington, DC 20001, 202-887-6791. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Upon acceptance to the program, applicants will be required to provide proof of a current, active, and unencumbered RN license in the State of residence. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">*Additionally, in the practicum courses, practicum sites may require students to provide evidence of current, active professional liability, malpractice insurance coverage for practicum courses, and provide evidence of a current AHA Healthcare Provider BLS CPR Card.\"</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For information about the program and how to obtain the RN to BSN Program application, students should email the Admissions Coordinator at </span><a href=\"mailto:RNCompletion@nu.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">RNCompletion@nu.edu</a></p>"
    }
  ],
