        "text": "General Information for Transfer Students",
        "links": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thank you for your interest in National University!\n National University, one of the largest private nonprofit universities in the United States, is committed to your success through our Whole Human Education approach. \n\nFlexible Learning on Your Terms\nNational University's flexible four and eight-week online courses allow you to focus on one class at a time. With unlimited free tutoring, individual coaching, and a dedicated writing center, we provide the support you need to excel. NU accepts and reviews applications year-round, so you can start your classes as soon as next month, depending on your program of study and location of choice. To learn more about applying, visit our Admissions page or call (855) 355-6288. \n \nAdditional Resources\n·      NU Course Equivalency Site: See how your other previous courses or exams will transfer to NU.\n·      ADT Degrees: Explore scholarship and degree pathways for CCC students with ADT degrees.\n·      Financial Aid: Discover how our Financial Aid team can help you secure the necessary resources.\n·      NU Catalog: For detailed policies and more information.",
